                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "User",
                    "login": "cemiu"
                  },
                  "body": "We could always maintain the dimensionality for both batch and non_tensor_batch, and then add a squeeze function to DataProto. However, int indices removing a dimension while slices maintain it is fairly common in Python (lists, numpy, torch, etc.) so it's not necessarily a bad thing.\r\n\r\nI am far too new to the code base to know what the appropriate call is though",
